46":[5,16,82],"47":[6,5,1],"48":[7,2,1],"49":[7,1,1],"50":[9,3,1],"51":[8,2,1],"52":[8,3,1],"53":[8,2,1],"54":[1,1,2],"55":[2,1,1],"56":[1,6,163],"57":[3,1,1],"58":[3,1,1],"59":[3,1,1],"60":[3,1,1],"61":[3,1,1],"62":[3,1,1]},"averageFieldLength":[4.650793650793651,3.1587301587301586,15.952380952380965],"storedFields":{"0":{"title":"Component Versions","id":"component-versions/","text":"Component Versions\n\n📦 Last updated: 8/20/2022\n\nService Versions\n\n\n\nService\nVersion\nRelease Date\nDocker Image\n\n\n\n\nThreeTwo (Main App)\n0.0.1\n8/20/2022\nfrishi/threetwo:0.0.1\n\n\nMetadata Service\n0.0.1\n8/20/2022\nfrishi/threetwo-metadata-service:0.0.1\n\n\nCore Service\n0.0.1\n8/20/2022\nfrishi/threetwo-core-service:0.0.1\n\n\nAcquisition Service\n0.0.1\n8/20/2022\nfrishi/threetwo-acquisition-service:0.0.1\n\n\n\nInstallation\nUsing Docker Compose\nWhen deploying, ensure you use compatible versions of all services together.\nservices:\n  threetwo:\n    image: frishi/threetwo:0.0.1\n\n  metadata-service:\n    image: frishi/threetwo-metadata-service:0.0.1\n\n  core-service:\n    image: frishi/threetwo-core-service:0.0.1\n\n  acquisition-service:\n    image: frishi/threetwo-acquisition-service:0.0.1\n\nVersion History\nFor compatibility information between versions, see\nCOMPATIBILITY.md.\nChecking Your Versions\nTo verify which versions are running in your deployment:\n# Check docker images in use\ndocker ps --format &quot;table {{.Names}}\\t{{.Image}}&quot;\n\n# Check running container versions\ndocker inspect &lt;container-name&gt; | grep -i version\n\nRelease Notes\n\nThreeTwo (Main App): v0.0.1\nMetadata Service: v0.0.1\nCore Service: v0.0.1\nAcquisition Service: v0.0.1\n\n","version":"Latest (Development)"},"1":{"title":"Component Versions > Component Versions","id":"component-versions/#component-versions","text":"","version":"Latest (Development)"},"2":{"title":"Component Versions > Service Versions","id":"component-versions/#component-versions-service-versions","text":"","version":"Latest (Development)"},"3":{"title":"Component Versions > Installation","id":"component-versions/#component-versions-installation","text":"","version":"Latest (Development)"},"4":{"title":"Component Versions > Using Docker Compose","id":"component-versions/#component-versions-installation-using-docker-compose","text":"","version":"Latest (Development)"},"5":{"title":"Component Versions > Version History","id":"component-versions/#component-versions-version-history","text":"","version":"Latest (Development)"},"6":{"title":"Component Versions > Checking Your Versions","id":"component-versions/#component-versions-checking-your-versions","text":"","version":"Latest (Development)"},"7":{"title":"Component Versions > Release Notes","id":"component-versions/#component-versions-release-notes","text":"","version":"Latest (Development)"},"8":{"title":"Installation","id":"installation/","text":"Installation\n","version":"Latest (Development)"},"9":{"title":"Installation > Installation","id":"installation/#installation","text":"","version":"Latest (Development)"},"10":{"title":"Introduction","id":"intro/","text":"ThreeTwo\nThreeTwo! is a comic book curation app.\nIt aims to help you organize your comic book collection and automate various\naspects of curating comics.\nIt is a culmination of ideas I developed over the past couple of years using\nvarious pieces of software to achieve the stated goal of curating comic books.\nIt borrows heavily from Mylar, Ubooquity, ComicRack, Calibre and many other\nsoftware used to manage comic book collections.\nPhilosophy\nWhether you collect comics because you are a hoarder, or you suffer from the\nvagaries of corporate greed, curation is solace. A safe space, meant for\ncollecting the artifacts that hold a special place in your heart. ThreeTwo\naspires to be the means to that end, nothing more.\nDiscovery\nThreeTwo encourages discovery by letting your comic collection take center stage.\nDiscovery is important, both from a technical perspective, so that ThreeTwo! can infer\nmetadata from your collection, as well as from a curatorial standpoint. Enjoy reading your\ncomics in-app, or just gawk at the beautiful cover art.\nCuration\nThreeTwo! takes curation seriously, and thusly offers ComicVine scraping,\namong other sources and helps enrich the comic metadata. This is so that your\ncollection can truly shine, and actually help in discovering or rediscovering\ncomics.\nAcquisition\nOnce you have added to your list of wanted comics, you can rely on\nThreeTwo!'s first-class support for DC++ via AirDC++ to acquire them.\nJust configure your AirDC++ host, hub information and you are golden.\nOf course, ThreeTwo does not and will never condone piracy or copyright infringement.\nConsumption\nYou can access your massive comic collection via OPDS through apps on your\nmobile devices, like Panels on iOS\n","version":"Latest (Development)"},"11":{"title":"Introduction > ThreeTwo","id":"intro/#threetwo","text":"","version":"Latest (Development)"},"12":{"title":"Introduction > Philosophy","id":"intro/#philosophy","text":"","version":"Latest (Development)"},"13":{"title":"Introduction > Discovery","id":"intro/#philosophy-discovery","text":"","version":"Latest (Development)"},"14":{"title":"Introduction > Curation","id":"intro/#philosophy-curation","text":"","version":"Latest (Development)"},"15":{"title":"Introduction > Acquisition","id":"intro/#philosophy-acquisition","text":"","version":"Latest (Development)"},"16":{"title":"Introduction > Consumption","id":"intro/#philosophy-consumption","text":"","version":"Latest (Development)"},"17":{"title":"Local Development","id":"local-development/","text":"Overview\nThreeTwo! is built on microservices. A compose.yaml brings the UI up along with the service dependencies.\nRepositories\nTo develop ThreeTwo! locally, begin by cloning these repositories to your machine:\n\nthreetwo - the main UI application\nthreetwo-metadata-service - Library management and core endpoints.\nthreetwo-core-service - Metadata related endpoints.\nthreetwo-acquisition-service - AirDC++ and other acquisition-related endpoints.\n\nPre-requisites\n\nLinux/macOS/Windows\ndocker compose or podman compose\nCreate 2 folders named userdata and comics inside threetwo-core-service folder.\nAirDC++ instance installed and running for DC++ downloads.\nqBittorrent instance installed and running for torrent downloads.\n\nSetting up dependencies (critical step)\nthreetwo-core-service comes with a dependencies.docker-compose.yml that has all the infrastructure for running the entire services stack.\nBring it up with:\ndocker system prune -af &amp;&amp; docker compose -f dependencies.docker-compose.yml up\n\nBring up the services, one by one\nExplanation of Environment Variables\nYou will see these vars in several startup commands. The following table explains what they are.\n\n\n\nEnvironment Variable\nExplanation\nRequired\nValue\n\n\n\n\nCOMICS_DIRECTORY\nfolder containing the comics\nYes\nSupply your own\n\n\nUSERDATA_DIRECTORY\nscratch folder\nYes\nSupply your own\n\n\nREDIS_URI\nRedis instance URI\nYes\nredis://127.0.0.1:6379\n\n\nELASTICSEARCH_URI\nElasticsearch instance URI\nYes\nhttp://localhost:9200\n\n\nKAFKA_BROKER\nKafka broker URI\nYes\nkafka1:9092\n\n\nUNRAR_BIN_PATH\nPath to unrar in the container\nYes\nSupply your own\n\n\nSEVENZ_BINARY_PATH\nPath to 7za in the container\nYes\nSupply your own\n\n\nCOMICVINE_API_KEY\nComicVine API Key\nYes\nSupply your own\n\n\n\nthreetwo-core-service\nBring up core service with:\nCOMICS_DIRECTORY=&lt;ABSOLUTE PATH TO COMICS DIRECTORY&gt; \\\nUSERDATA_DIRECTORY=&lt;ABSOLUTE PATH TO USERDATA DIRECTORY&gt; \\\nREDIS_URI=redis://127.0.0.1:6379 \\\nELASTICSEARCH_URI=http://localhost:9200 \\\nMONGO_URI=mongodb://localhost:27017/threetwo \\\nKAFKA_BROKER=kafka1:9092 \\\nUNRAR_BIN_PATH=/opt/homebrew/bin/unrar \\\nSEVENZ_BINARY_PATH=/opt/homebrew/bin/7za \\\nnpm run dev\n\nthreetwo-metadata-service\nCOMICVINE_API_KEY=&lt;YOUR COMICVINE API KEY&gt; \\\nREDIS_URI=redis://127.0.0.1:6379 \\\nUSERDATA_DIRECTORY=&lt;ABSOLUTE PATH TO USERDATA DIRECTORY&gt; \\\nnpm run dev\n\nthreetwo-acquisition-service\nKAFKA_BROKER=kafka1:9092 npm run dev\n\nBring up the UI\nFrom within the threetwo folder, simply run:\nyarn dev\n\nContributing\nOnce your local environment is up and running, feel free to open a pull\nrequest against the relevant repository. If you run into issues setting\nthings up, reach out on Discord or open an\nissue on the corresponding repo.\n","version":"Latest (Development)"},"18":{"title":"Local Development > Overview","id":"local-development/#overview","text":"","version":"Latest (Development)"},"19":{"title":"Local Development > Repositories","id":"local-development/#repositories","text":"","version":"Latest (Development)"},"20":{"title":"Local Development > Pre-requisites","id":"local-development/#pre-requisites","text":"","version":"Latest (Development)"},"21":{"title":"Local Development > Setting up dependencies (critical step)","id":"local-development/#setting-up-dependencies-critical-step","text":"","version":"Latest (Development)"},"22":{"title":"Local Development > Bring up the services, one by one","id":"local-development/#bring-up-the-services-one-by-one","text":"","version":"Latest (Development)"},"23":{"title":"Local Development > Explanation of Environment Variables","id":"local-development/#bring-up-the-services-one-by-one-explanation-of-environment-variables","text":"","version":"Latest (Development)"},"24":{"title":"Local Development > threetwo-core-service","id":"local-development/#bring-up-the-services-one-by-one-threetwo-core-service","text":"","version":"Latest (Development)"},"25":{"title":"Local Development > threetwo-metadata-service","id":"local-development/#bring-up-the-services-one-by-one-threetwo-metadata-service","text":"","version":"Latest (Development)"},"26":{"title":"Local Development > threetwo-acquisition-service","id":"local-development/#bring-up-the-services-one-by-one-threetwo-acquisition-service","text":"","version":"Latest (Development)"},"27":{"title":"Local Development > Bring up the UI","id":"local-development/#bring-up-the-ui","text":"","version":"Latest (Development)"},"28":{"title":"Local Development > Contributing","id":"local-development/#contributing","text":"","version":"Latest (Development)"},"29":{"title":"Component Versions - v0.0.1-beta","id":"v0.0.1-beta/component-versions/","text":"Component Versions - v0.0.1-beta\n\n📦 Last updated: 8/20/2022\n\nService Versions\n\n\n\nService\nVersion\nRelease Date\nDocker Image\n\n\n\n\nThreeTwo (Main App)\n0.0.1\n8/20/2022\nfrishi/threetwo:0.0.1\n\n\nMetadata Service\n0.0.1\n8/20/2022\nfrishi/threetwo-metadata-service:0.0.1\n\n\nCore Service\n0.0.1\n8/20/2022\nfrishi/threetwo-core-service:0.0.1\n\n\nAcquisition Service\n0.0.1\n8/20/2022\nfrishi/threetwo-acquisition-service:0.0.1\n\n\n\nInstallation\nUsing Docker Compose\nWhen deploying, ensure you use compatible versions of all services together.\nservices:\n  threetwo:\n    image: frishi/threetwo:0.0.1\n\n  metadata-service:\n    image: frishi/threetwo-metadata-service:0.0.1\n\n  core-service:\n    image: frishi/threetwo-core-service:0.0.1\n\n  acquisition-service:\n    image: frishi/threetwo-acquisition-service:0.0.1\n\nVersion History\nFor compatibility information between versions, see\nCOMPATIBILITY.md.\nChecking Your Versions\nTo verify which versions are running in your deployment:\n# Check docker images in use\ndocker ps --format &quot;table {{.Names}}\\t{{.Image}}&quot;\n\n# Check running container versions\ndocker inspect &lt;container-name&gt; | grep -i version\n\nRelease Notes\n\nThreeTwo (Main App): v0.0.1\nMetadata Service: v0.0.1\nCore Service: v0.0.1\nAcquisition Service: v0.0.1\n\n","version":"v0.0.1-beta"},"30":{"title":"Component Versions - v0.0.1-beta > Component Versions - v0.0.1-beta","id":"v0.0.1-beta/component-versions/#component-versions-v001-beta","text":"","version":"v0.0.1-beta"},"31":{"title":"Component Versions - v0.0.1-beta > Service Versions","id":"v0.0.1-beta/component-versions/#component-versions-v001-beta-service-versions","text":"","version":"v0.0.1-beta"},"32":{"title":"Component Versions - v0.0.1-beta > Installation","id":"v0.0.1-beta/component-versions/#component-versions-v001-beta-installation","text":"","version":"v0.0.1-beta"},"33":{"title":"Component Versions - v0.0.1-beta > Using Docker Compose","id":"v0.0.1-beta/component-versions/#component-versions-v001-beta-installation-using-docker-compose","text":"","version":"v0.0.1-beta"},"34":{"title":"Component Versions - v0.0.1-beta > Version History","id":"v0.0.1-beta/component-versions/#component-versions-v001-beta-version-history","text":"","version":"v0.0.1-beta"},"35":{"title":"Component Versions - v0.0.1-beta > Checking Your Versions","id":"v0.0.1-beta/component-versions/#component-versions-v001-beta-checking-your-versions","text":"","version":"v0.0.1-beta"},"36":{"title":"Component Versions - v0.0.1-beta > Release Notes","id":"v0.0.1-beta/component-versions/#component-versions-v001-beta-release-notes","text":"","version":"v0.0.1-beta"},"37":{"title":"Installation","id":"v0.0.1-beta/installation/","text":"Installation\n","version":"v0.0.1-beta"},"38":{"title":"Installation > Installation","id":"v0.0.1-beta/installation/#installation","text":"","version":"v0.0.1-beta"},"39":{"title":"Introduction","id":"v0.0.1-beta/intro/","text":"ThreeTwo\nThreeTwo! is a comic book curation app.\nIt aims to help you organize your comic book collection and automate various\naspects of curating comics.\nIt is a culmination of ideas I developed over the past couple of years using\nvarious pieces of software to achieve the stated goal of curating comic books.\nIt borrows heavily from Mylar, Ubooquity, ComicRack, Calibre and many other\nsoftware used to manage comic book collections.\nPhilosophy\nWhether you collect comics because you are a hoarder, or you suffer from the\nvagaries of corporate greed, curation is a solace. A safe space, meant for\ncollecting the artifacts that hold a special place in your heart. ThreeTwo\naspires to be the means to that end, nothing more.\nDiscovery\nThe first tenet of ThreeTwo! is discovery–the act of importing comics from\nyour OS, finding new comic to read or just searching through your collection\nfor a comic that sparks nostalgia. Discovery is important, both from a\ntechnical perspective, so that ThreeTwo! can infer metadata from your\ncollection, as well as from a curatorial standpoint, you want to keep track of\nwhat you are reading, or what you want to be reading.\nCuration\nThreeTwo! takes curation seriously, and thusly offers ComicVine scraping, and\nother means of applying/extending the comic metadata. This is so that your\ncollection can truly shine, and actually help in discovering or rediscovering\ncomics.\nAcquisition\nOnce you have added to your list of wanted comics, you can rely on\nThreeTwo!'s first-class support for DC++ via AirDC++ to acquire them.\nJust configure your AirDC++ host, hub information and you are golden.\nConsumption\nYou can access your massive comic collection via OPDS through apps on your\nmobile devices, like Panels on iOS\n","version":"v0.0.1-beta"},"40":{"title":"Introduction > ThreeTwo","id":"v0.0.1-beta/intro/#threetwo","text":"","version":"v0.0.1-beta"},"41":{"title":"Introduction > Philosophy","id":"v0.0.1-beta/intro/#philosophy","text":"","version":"v0.0.1-beta"},"42":{"title":"Introduction > Discovery","id":"v0.0.1-beta/intro/#philosophy-discovery","text":"","version":"v0.0.1-beta"},"43":{"title":"Introduction > Curation","id":"v0.0.1-beta/intro/#philosophy-curation","text":"","version":"v0.0.1-beta"},"44":{"title":"Introduction > Acquisition","id":"v0.0.1-beta/intro/#philosophy-acquisition","text":"","version":"v0.0.1-beta"},"45":{"title":"Introduction > Consumption","id":"v0.0.1-beta/intro/#philosophy-consumption","text":"","version":"v0.0.1-beta"},"46":{"title":"Component Versions - v0.0.1","id":"v0.0.1/component-versions/","text":"Component Versions - v0.0.1\n\n📦 Last updated: 8/20/2022\n\nService Versions\n\n\n\nService\nVersion\nRelease Date\nDocker Image\n\n\n\n\nThreeTwo (Main App)\n0.0.1\n8/20/2022\nfrishi/threetwo:0.0.1\n\n\nMetadata Service\n0.0.1\n8/20/2022\nfrishi/threetwo-metadata-service:0.0.1\n\n\nCore Service\n0.0.1\n8/20/2022\nfrishi/threetwo-core-service:0.0.1\n\n\nAcquisition Service\n0.0.1\n8/20/2022\nfrishi/threetwo-acquisition-service:0.0.1\n\n\n\nInstallation\nUsing Docker Compose\nWhen deploying, ensure you use compatible versions of all services together.\nservices:\n  threetwo:\n    image: frishi/threetwo:0.0.1\n\n  metadata-service:\n    image: frishi/threetwo-metadata-service:0.0.1\n\n  core-service:\n    image: frishi/threetwo-core-service:0.0.1\n\n  acquisition-service:\n    image: frishi/threetwo-acquisition-service:0.0.1\n\nVersion History\nFor compatibility information between versions, see\nCOMPATIBILITY.md.\nChecking Your Versions\nTo verify which versions are running in your deployment:\n# Check docker images in use\ndocker ps --format &quot;table {{.Names}}\\t{{.Image}}&quot;\n\n# Check running container versions\ndocker inspect &lt;container-name&gt; | grep -i version\n\nRelease Notes\n\nThreeTwo (Main App): v0.0.1\nMetadata Service: v0.0.1\nCore Service: v0.0.1\nAcquisition Service: v0.0.1\n\n","version":"v0.0.1"},"47":{"title":"Component Versions - v0.0.1 > Component Versions - v0.0.1","id":"v0.0.1/component-versions/#component-versions-v001","text":"","version":"v0.0.1"},"48":{"title":"Component Versions - v0.0.1 > Service Versions","id":"v0.0.1/component-versions/#component-versions-v001-service-versions","text":"","version":"v0.0.1"},"49":{"title":"Component Versions - v0.0.1 > Installation","id":"v0.0.1/component-versions/#component-versions-v001-installation","text":"","version":"v0.0.1"},"50":{"title":"Component Versions - v0.0.1 > Using Docker Compose","id":"v0.0.1/component-versions/#component-versions-v001-installation-using-docker-compose","text":"","version":"v0.0.1"},"51":{"title":"Component Versions - v0.0.1 > Version History","id":"v0.0.1/component-versions/#component-versions-v001-version-history","text":"","version":"v0.0.1"},"52":{"title":"Component Versions - v0.0.1 > Checking Your Versions","id":"v0.0.1/component-versions/#component-versions-v001-checking-your-versions","text":"","version":"v0.0.1"},"53":{"title":"Component Versions - v0.0.1 > Release Notes","id":"v0.0.1/component-versions/#component-versions-v001-release-notes","text":"","version":"v0.0.1"},"54":{"title":"Installation","id":"v0.0.1/installation/","text":"Installation\n","version":"v0.0.1"},"55":{"title":"Installation > Installation","id":"v0.0.1/installation/#installation","text":"","version":"v0.0.1"},"56":{"title":"Introduction","id":"v0.0.1/intro/","text":"ThreeTwo\nThreeTwo! is a comic book curation app.\nIt aims to help you organize your comic book collection and automate various\naspects of curating comics.\nIt is a culmination of ideas I developed over the past couple of years using\nvarious pieces of software to achieve the stated goal of curating comic books.\nIt borrows heavily from Mylar, Ubooquity, ComicRack, Calibre and many other\nsoftware used to manage comic book collections.\nPhilosophy\nWhether you collect comics because you are a hoarder, or you suffer from the\nvagaries of corporate greed, curation is a solace. A safe space, meant for\ncollecting the artifacts that hold a special place in your heart. ThreeTwo\naspires to be the means to that end, nothing more.\nDiscovery\nThe first tenet of ThreeTwo! is discovery–the act of importing comics from\nyour OS, finding new comic to read or just searching through your collection\nfor a comic that sparks nostalgia. Discovery is important, both from a\ntechnical perspective, so that ThreeTwo! can infer metadata from your\ncollection, as well as from a curatorial standpoint, you want to keep track of\nwhat you are reading, or what you want to be reading.\nCuration\nThreeTwo! takes curation seriously, and thusly offers ComicVine scraping, and\nother means of applying/extending the comic metadata. This is so that your\ncollection can truly shine, and actually help in discovering or rediscovering\ncomics.\nAcquisition\nOnce you have added to your list of wanted comics, you can rely on\nThreeTwo!'s first-class support for DC++ via AirDC++ to acquire them.\nJust configure your AirDC++ host, hub information and you are golden.\nConsumption\nYou can access your massive comic collection via OPDS through apps on your\nmobile devices, like Panels on iOS\n","version":"v0.0.1"},"57":{"title":"Introduction > ThreeTwo","id":"v0.0.1/intro/#threetwo","text":"","version":"v0.0.1"},"58":{"title":"Introduction > Philosophy","id":"v0.0.1/intro/#philosophy","text":"","version":"v0.0.1"},"59":{"title":"Introduction > Discovery","id":"v0.0.1/intro/#philosophy-discovery","text":"","version":"v0.0.1"},"60":{"title":"Introduction > Curation","id":"v0.0.1/intro/#philosophy-curation","text":"","version":"v0.0.1"},"61":{"title":"Introduction > Acquisition","id":"v0.0.1/intro/#philosophy-acquisition","text":"","version":"v0.0.1"},"62":{"title":"Introduction > Consumption","id":"v0.0.1/intro/#philosophy-consumption","text":"","version":"v0.0.1"}},"dirtCount":0,"index":[["keep",{"2":{"39":1,"56":1}}],["key=",{"2":{"17":1}}],["key",{"2":{"17":3}}],["kafka1",{"2":{"17":1}}],["kafka",{"2":{"17":4}}],["7za",{"2":{"17":2}}],["9092",{"2":{"17":3}}],["9200",{"2":{"17":2}}],["6379",{"2":{"17":3}}],["qbittorrent",{"2":{"17":1}}],["quot",{"2":{"0":2,"29":2,"46":2}}],["27017",{"2":{"17":1}}],["2",{"2":{"17":1}}],["2022",{"2":{"0":5,"29":5,"46":5}}],["20",{"2":{"0":5,"29":5,"46":5}}],["extending",{"2":{"39":1,"56":1}}],["explains",{"2":{"17":1}}],["explanation",{"0":{"23":1},"1":{"17":1,"23":1},"2":{"17":2}}],["elasticsearch",{"2":{"17":3}}],["entire",{"2":{"17":1}}],["environment",{"0":{"23":1},"1